          html: `<p class="lead">A <b>solid</b> has three dimensions: length, breadth and thickness. On a flat sheet, which has only length and breadth, a solid needs <b>two or more orthographic views</b>.</p>
<p>Projection of solids represents 3-D objects on 2-D drawing planes. It helps to visualise the size and form of objects, communicate sizes and features, prepare manufacturing drawings, and support design, analysis and CAD modelling.</p>
<div class="note why"><p>One view never shows the true shape and size of a solid. A frustum of a pyramid looks like a trapezium from the front and like two squares from the top; you need both.</p></div>`
