          html: `<div class="vs"><div class="side"><h4>Polyhedra</h4><p>Bounded only by <b>plane (flat) faces</b>; edges where faces meet. When all faces are equal and regular, the polyhedron is <b>regular</b>.</p><p>Tetrahedron (4 triangular faces), cube or hexahedron (6 square faces), prisms, pyramids.</p></div><div class="side"><h4>Solids of revolution</h4><p>Generated by <b>rotating a plane figure about a fixed axis</b> through 360°. They have curved surfaces.</p><p>Cylinder (rectangle about one side), cone (right triangle about one side), sphere (semicircle about its diameter).</p></div></div>
<table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Solid</th><th>Definition</th><th>Named by</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Prism</td><td>Two equal and parallel polygonal bases joined by rectangular faces</td><td>Shape of the base: triangular, square, pentagonal, hexagonal</td></tr>
<tr><td>Pyramid</td><td>One polygonal base and triangular faces meeting at a point, the apex</td><td>Shape of the base</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>A <b>right</b> (regular) solid has its axis perpendicular to its base; an <b>oblique</b> solid has its axis inclined.</p>`
